# F-Droid MR updates (agents)

Details: [`metadata/FDROID_SUBMISSION.md`](metadata/FDROID_SUBMISSION.md).
Release order: [`docs/RELEASING.md`](docs/RELEASING.md).

## Open MRs (first listing still open)

| App | MR | Fork branch |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Link | [!50470](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroiddata/-/merge_requests/50470) | `new/kinetic-link-0.4.1` |
| Kids | [!50471](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroiddata/-/merge_requests/50471) | `new/kinetic-kids-0.4.1` |

One app per MR until both are merged upstream. Pipelines run on the **fork**
(`ingmarstruijs/fdroiddata`), not only on `fdroid/fdroiddata`.

## What to push

- **Only** `metadata/net.moonbaseone.kinetic.{link,kids}.yml`
- Never Fastlane, screenshots, or other Kinetic tree paths
- Source of truth: this repo’s `metadata/*.yml` after the GitHub release is green
- `commit:` = full SHA of annotated `vX.Y.Z` (not the tag name)
- ABI codes for pubspec `+N`: `N*10+1` / `+2` / `+3` → highest is
  `CurrentVersionCode`

## Builds: ADD new versions, never REPLACE (live apps)

For an app **already on f-droid.org** (Kids) or any **update MR**:

- **ADD** three new `Builds:` blocks for the new ABI codes
- **Keep** every existing older `Builds:` block (e.g. keep 0.4.6 `161/162/163`
  when adding 0.4.7 `171/172/173`)
- Only bump `CurrentVersion` / `CurrentVersionCode` to the new suggested release
- Do **not** delete or overwrite previous version blocks — maintainers reject
  REPLACE (`@licaon-kter`: “ADD build blocks for new versions, not REPLACE”)

Exception: a **first-listing** “New app” MR may keep only the latest version
blocks until merge (inclusion checklist). After the app is live, always ADD.

## Before `git push` to GitLab

1. Confirm GitHub Releases exist: `vX.Y.Z-link` and `vX.Y.Z-kids`
2. Normalize YAML to LF; trim so file ends with one newline after last key
3. Prefer writing bytes explicitly on Windows (PowerShell redirect can be UTF-16)
4. Do not leave an empty line after `CurrentVersionCode` (`rewritemeta` fails)

## After push

1. Watch fork pipelines until `fdroid rewritemeta`, `checkupdates`, and
   `fdroid build` finish (failed early jobs can leave the pipeline “running”)
2. Update MR description from `metadata/FDROID_MR_BODY_{link,kids}.md` if the
   version/commit story changed; reply to open review threads
3. Do not mark “all pipelines should pass” until the latest pipeline is green

## Local dirty fork

If checkout fails (`index.lock`, untracked YAML on the wrong branch): clean the
untracked file, remove the lock, pull the target branch, then copy YAML again.
Never commit Link YAML onto the Kids branch (or the reverse).
